      "eng_exp": "Use comparative adjectives to compare two people or things. We usually add -er to the adjective and use the word than. Use superlative adjectives to compare three or more people or things. We usually add the before the adjective and -est to the end. Rule for long words: If an adjective has more than two syllables, use more for comparative, and the most for superlative. Spelling Rule: For adjectives ending in y, change the y to i and add -er or -est. 4, 6",
